data_case_b_network
#
# Case B: Asp30 and His35 on one short poly-ALA chain flip together as one network, 50/50.
# net_1 = {Asp30 A, His35 A}, net_2 = {Asp30 B, His35 B}; one occupancy group 'rotamer' under
# base. The altloc letter alone cannot say that the two residues' A conformers are ONE state --
# that cross-residue correlation is exactly what pdbx_alt_groups records. Only the two side
# chains carry the A/B alternates; the backbone and flanking ALA are single-conformer (altloc '.').
#
